## Architecture
- **26 Astro route files**; current release build generates 33 static HTML pages (Astro 6, static output only, no SSR)
- **8 interactive tools** (all client-side compute, no external deps)
- **13 src/lib domain folders** with 500 unit tests at 100% coverage
- **Admin panel** behind Cloudflare Access (Zero Trust)
- **CV** gated via email capture + admin review + Resend delivery
- **CSP** dual-layer: `scripts/generate-headers.ts` + `BaseLayout.astro` meta tag

### Data Flow
```
src/data/*.ts → src/lib/ → src/pages/*.astro → dist/ → Cloudflare CDN
```

### Tool Pattern
```
src/lib/<tool>/   (data + logic + tests)  ← backend-engineer
src/pages/tools/<slug>.astro (UI + script) ← frontend-engineer
```

## Agent Instruction Surfaces
- `AGENTS.md` is the compact operating contract.
- `CLAUDE.md` is the full repo onboarding guide.
- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` are Cursor-specific rules.
- `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` are Codex skills; frontmatter must be valid YAML.
- `.codex/agents/*.toml` are repo-local sub-agent role cards.
- `.codex/config.toml` is runtime config only. Do not add `[instructions]` or `developer_instructions` tables; that shape breaks Codex skill reload.

## Code Rules
- No `any` types — explicit types on all public APIs
- No comments unless WHY is non-obvious
- No onclick/inline handlers (Cloudflare Rocket Loader)
- `data-cfasync="false"` on all `<script is:inline>`
- 100% test coverage on `src/data/` and `src/lib/`
- No external runtime dependencies for tools
- Minimal diffs — don't refactor adjacent code

## Engineering Skill Defaults
- Use `debug-mantra` for bug reports, failing checks, regressions, stack traces, or broken behavior before proposing fixes.
- Use `scrutinize` for plan review, PR review, diff review, architecture/design sanity checks, and second-opinion review.
- Use `post-mortem` only after there is a reliable repro, known root cause, implemented fix, and validation evidence.
- When Codex hands work to Cursor, follow the skill lens named in the `.tmp/*-handoff.md`.
- For Codex-managed Cursor work, Cursor runs the requested verification commands, including `bun run check` when full confidence is needed; Codex reviews Cursor's output and reruns tests only if evidence is incomplete or the user asks.

## Implementation Lane
- Default code implementation to `codex-spark` for bounded build/edit work when available.
- Switch back to the smarter Codex lane when `codex-spark` is buggy, misses repo rules, cannot produce production-grade output, or the work is high-risk/complex.
- Codex remains accountable for planning, review, verification evidence, and final acceptance regardless of implementation lane.

## Content Writing Defaults
- Use the repo-local `technical_writer` sub-agent lens when starting, outlining, drafting, or reviewing public content: blog posts, technical docs, release notes, page copy, metadata, references, and related-tool CTAs.
- For blog work, pair `technical_writer` with `blog-content-strategy` and `document-writer`; use `product-manager` first when topic selection or business rationale is still open.
- Writer output must preserve xhverse voice: practical, peer-facing, source-backed, no vendor hype, no invented private client claims.

## Git Workflow
- Branch from `development` — never `main`
- **NEVER** edit on `development` or `main` — create branch first
- All PRs target `development`
- Release: `development` → `main` PR → annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` with a useful message → GitHub Release
- Verify in browser (both themes, mobile) before pushing
- QA + Security gate every release

## Commands
```bash
bun run check        # Full pipeline (typecheck + build + coverage + e2e)
bun run dev          # Dev server at localhost:4321
bun run typecheck    # Type checks (0 errors required)
bun run coverage     # Tests + 100% enforcement
bun run test:e2e     # Playwright (30 tests, chromium + mobile)
bun run build        # Production build (33 generated pages in v3.7.1)
```

## Implementation Rules
- Prefer minimal, production-grade diffs
- Preserve existing behavior unless task explicitly requires change
- Do not modify: `coverage/`, `dist/`, `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`, `.astro/`
- Do not touch `supabase/` migrations unless explicitly asked
- For complex tasks, produce a plan first
- Show user in browser before pushing — no exceptions

## Design System (dark-first)
- Background: `bg-[var(--bg-page)]`
- Text: white (headings), zinc-300/400 (body), zinc-500 (labels)
- Accent: emerald-200/300 (CTAs, active, positive)
- Static cards: `static-card` or muted border/bg treatment with no hover lift, pointer cursor, or CTA arrow
- Interactive cards: semantic `<a>`/`<button>` with `interactive-card`, visible focus state, hover/focus feedback, and link cue
- CTAs: `cta-primary` for primary actions, `cta-secondary` for supporting actions
- Text links: recognizable underline treatment; mark external links with `external-link` where appropriate
- Labels: `text-[10-12px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em]`
- Container: `max-w-7xl px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10`

## Reports
- Keep concise
- Report only what was actually changed or verified
- Do not claim checks were run unless explicitly run
